WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.683
In this video, we'll add a practice FAQ, from a blank form to a live page.

00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:11.810
Along the way we'll use every formatting tool once, so you can see what each one does.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.239
Open FAQs, and click New FAQ.

00:00:15.239 --> 00:00:19.690
You can also use Quick add, at the top right.

00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:21.608
A blank FAQ opens.

00:00:21.608 --> 00:00:27.523
The fields are on the left, and the preview on the right fills in as you type.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.414
First, the topic.

00:00:29.414 --> 00:00:33.650
Click the box, and pick the topic this FAQ belongs to.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.160
You can type to filter the list.

00:00:36.714 --> 00:00:38.029
Next, the question.

00:00:38.029 --> 00:00:43.218
Write it in full, with its question mark, exactly as readers should see it.

00:00:43.218 --> 00:00:49.514
It also sets the page's web address, so get it right before you publish for the first time.

00:00:50.066 --> 00:00:54.472
Display order decides where it sits in the topic's list.

00:00:54.472 --> 00:00:56.439
Lower numbers come first.

00:00:56.439 --> 00:01:02.103
Number in tens, ten, twenty, thirty, so you can slot a new FAQ in later.

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:06.666
For practice, we'll use ninety-nine, to put it at the end.

00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:08.540
Now switch Draft on.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:15.817
You can publish as often as you like while you write, and nothing appears on the site until you switch it off.

00:01:16.373 --> 00:01:22.510
Related FAQs and Related videos add a Related Resources box at the foot of the page.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:23.752
They're optional.

00:01:23.752 --> 00:01:27.552
Start typing a question, then pick the one you want.

00:01:27.552 --> 00:01:29.013
You can add several.

00:01:29.576 --> 00:01:31.543
Videos work the same way.

00:01:31.543 --> 00:01:33.667
Chosen links show as chips.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:36.736
Click the cross on a chip to remove it.

00:01:37.302 --> 00:01:38.623
Now the answer.

00:01:38.623 --> 00:01:49.982
Its toolbar has bold, italic and the other text styles, a link button, headings, quotes and lists, and Add Component, for images.

00:01:50.538 --> 00:01:53.233
Write as you would in a word processor.

00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:55.236
Enter starts a new paragraph.

00:01:55.236 --> 00:02:01.178
If you paste from Word or Google Docs, check the formatting in the preview afterwards.

00:02:01.731 --> 00:02:06.182
For a section heading, open Headings and choose Heading 2.

00:02:06.182 --> 00:02:08.100
Use Heading 3 below that.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:13.011
Never use Heading 1: the question is already the page's heading.

00:02:13.562 --> 00:02:19.362
Bold works as usual: click Bold, type, and click it again to stop.

00:02:21.561 --> 00:02:24.623
To add a link, select the words first.

00:02:24.623 --> 00:02:26.798
Then click the link button.

00:02:26.798 --> 00:02:29.457
A small box asks for the address.

00:02:29.457 --> 00:02:34.130
Paste the full address, starting with https, and click OK.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.481
Links to other websites open in a new tab on the site.

00:02:39.037 --> 00:02:44.917
For a list, click Bulleted list, and press Enter twice to finish it.

00:02:45.644 --> 00:02:48.250
Before adding an image, prepare it.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:54.950
It should be eight hundred to twelve hundred pixels wide, and under two hundred kilobytes.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.524
Use a JPG for photographs, and a PNG for charts.

00:02:59.091 --> 00:03:02.323
Click Add Component, and choose Image.

00:03:02.323 --> 00:03:05.811
An image block appears inside the answer.

00:03:06.364 --> 00:03:07.981
Click Choose an image.

00:03:07.981 --> 00:03:09.744
The image library opens.

00:03:09.744 --> 00:03:15.844
Click Upload to add a picture from your computer, or pick one that's already there.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.591
Your upload is selected.

00:03:18.591 --> 00:03:20.600
Click Choose selected.

00:03:21.181 --> 00:03:22.554
Then the alt text.

00:03:22.554 --> 00:03:29.268
This is what a blind reader hears in place of the picture, and what search engines read.

00:03:29.268 --> 00:03:33.006
Describe what the image shows and its main point.

00:03:33.006 --> 00:03:35.981
Chart, or the file name, is not enough.

00:03:36.541 --> 00:03:38.821
The title is optional.

00:03:39.616 --> 00:03:42.144
Never upload a picture of a table.

00:03:42.144 --> 00:03:46.827
A picture can't be read aloud, searched, or resized on a phone.

00:03:46.827 --> 00:03:53.369
Instead, paste the image into ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini, and ask for a plain HTML table.

00:03:53.369 --> 00:03:56.046
The exact prompt is in the handbook.

00:03:56.046 --> 00:04:02.216
Check the numbers against the original, because AI tools sometimes misread a digit.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.481
To paste it in, flip the answer's switch from Rich Text to Markdown.

00:04:07.481 --> 00:04:09.900
The answer now shows as plain text.

00:04:10.455 --> 00:04:13.526
Click where the table should go, and paste.

00:04:13.526 --> 00:04:20.095
This is also where you add the source line under an image: in italics, starting with Source.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:22.278
Flip back to Rich Text.

00:04:22.278 --> 00:04:26.501
The table's code stays visible as plain lines in the editor.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:27.486
That's normal.

00:04:27.486 --> 00:04:30.794
The preview, and the site, show a proper table.

00:04:30.794 --> 00:04:33.539
Edit those lines only in Markdown mode.

00:04:34.094 --> 00:04:35.047
Now publish.

00:04:35.047 --> 00:04:37.828
The Publish menu has three choices.

00:04:37.828 --> 00:04:40.052
Publish now saves the entry.

00:04:40.052 --> 00:04:45.374
The other two also open a blank entry, or a copy, to carry on with.

00:04:45.954 --> 00:04:47.554
Choose Publish now.

00:04:47.554 --> 00:04:53.114
The status reads Changes saved, and the button now says Published.

00:04:53.916 --> 00:04:58.581
Because Draft is on, the page doesn't exist on the site yet.

00:04:58.581 --> 00:05:02.236
Readers who try its address see Page not found.

00:05:02.953 --> 00:05:05.913
When the FAQ is ready, switch Draft off.

00:05:05.913 --> 00:05:10.353
The status turns to Unsaved changes until you publish again.

00:05:10.918 --> 00:05:13.838
Publish now, once more.

00:05:17.528 --> 00:05:19.328
And here it is on the site.

00:05:19.328 --> 00:05:24.061
On the live site this takes about two minutes, while the site rebuilds.

00:05:24.061 --> 00:05:27.128
Read it through once, to check it looks right.

00:05:27.846 --> 00:05:33.249
It also appears in the topic's list of FAQs, in the place its display order gives it.

00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:39.606
Each FAQ also gets its own share card automatically, the picture shown when someone shares the link.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:45.230
Next: editing, hiding and deleting an FAQ.
